 **Candidate 5:** good 2-day ordering for product 1, but product 0 only every 4 days. In total it holds as much stock as a 3-day plan while paying for 4 extra orders.\n\n**3. Order size, for the 3-day plans.** These plans never react to actual demand, so leftovers build up.\n- **Product 1:** running short costs about 13 a unit (lost margin 6 plus penalty 7). A surplus costs roughly 6 a unit plus holding. The best order is a little above mean demand, about +5%.\n- **Product 0:** the losses either way are about equal, so the best order is close to the mean.\n- **Candidate 1:** product 1 at about +5%, product 0 close to the mean (a bit low on days 3 and 6). The best of the 3-day plans.\n- **Candidate 4:** product 1 is about 15% over the mean, which means expiry losses and a warehouse near the limit around day 26. Product 0 is a bit high, which is fine.\n- **Candidate 3:** both products slightly below the mean.\n- **Candidate 7:** product 1 is too high, as in candidate 4, and product 0 is about 10% too low, so it runs short.\n\nCandidates 4 and 3 are close. I put 4 slightly ahead because running short of product 1 costs more than a surplus."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4816, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2313, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4816}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T22:59:40.205Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVTqURpqJaTfjkGAJxpV"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_015JnitzvrgJGcTB8rxjhDjB", "name": "Struct